From cd68271aaa36275e1abb8e6b4082cb5a90df1980 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicola Nicodemo <nicola084@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:51:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa: describe the CPUs' capacity

Without capacity-dmips-mhz, arch_topology computes no CPU capacities and
every CPU stays at 1024, although the second and third clusters reach
4012.8 MHz (boost) and the first only 3417.6 MHz. Single-threaded work then
lands on the first cluster as often as elsewhere: on the Galaxy Book4 Edge
Geekbench 7 single-core scored 2200 unpinned and 2482 pinned to CPUs 4-11.

All twelve cores are the same Oryon core, so give them the same
capacity-dmips-mhz; arch_topology scales it by each policy's maximum
frequency (cpuinfo.max_freq at policy creation), so the first cluster ends
up at ~872 and the others at 1024.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ALoC6yerK2c2q13o4h7F4t
---
